  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1600.html",
  "prefLabel": "Plc 1605.02 Notification of Pending Registration Expiration",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Plc 1605.02 Notification of Pending Registration Expiration.\n\n(a) At least 60 days prior to the expiration of a registration issued pursuant to RSA 326-M and Plc 1600, the licensing bureau shall:\n\n(1) Notify, in writing to the email address on file, each registrant whose registration is expiring that:\n\na. The registration is due to expire; and\n\nb. Failure to file a complete and timely application for renewal shall result in the registration expiring; and\n\n(2) Include with the written notice a copy of the application identified in Plc 1605.03 or, when the application is available on-line, a registration code, if one is necessary, to use to renew on-line.\n\n(b) A registrant who wishes to renew a registration who does not receive an application or registration code shall contact OPLC customer support at CustomerSupport@oplc.nh.gov to obtain an application or registration code, as applicable.\n\n(c) As provided in RSA 310:8, II and RSA 541-A:30, I, if a timely and complete renewal application has been filed then the registration shall continue as valid until final action is taken on the application for renewal.\n\n(d) A nurse agency whose registration has expired shall not operate as a nurse agency for compensation in New Hampshire unless and until the registration has been reinstated as provided in Plc 1605.11.\n\nSource. #13914, eff 5-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/plc1600.html"
